From: Sean Phan <seanphan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] path3: fix hc_attn_fn_broadcast never finalized for real
 weight loads

Attempt 3 crashed with AssertionError: self.hc_attn_fn_broadcast is not
None, in DeepseekV4DecoderLayer.forward (first layer, no-residual path),
during profile_run's image dummy-forward.

Root cause, found by diffing the in-image nvidia/model.py and vl_model.py
against the pinned Vision head (2c8af219ce4b79ce3285724b9a9c69d3f878116):

- vl_model.py's DeepseekV4ForConditionalGeneration.load_weights delegates
  to the child DeepseekV4ForCausalLM.load_weights via AutoWeightsLoader,
  then unconditionally sets `self._weights_finalized = True`, on the
  documented assumption that "the child's load_weights already ran its
  post-load finalization."
- In the pinned reference, DeepseekV4ForCausalLM.load_weights does call
  self.process_weights_after_loading() (which calls
  finalize_mega_moe_weights/finalize_mhc_broadcast_weights) right before
  returning -- matching that assumption.
- In this fork's ported nvidia/model.py, DeepseekV4ForCausalLM.load_weights
  did NOT call process_weights_after_loading() -- it only ran the
  AutoWeightsLoader and returned. So the wrapper's `_weights_finalized`
  flag was set to True regardless, and the wrapper's own
  process_weights_after_loading() (the only other place these finalize
  calls could happen) then early-returned on that flag and skipped them
  entirely. hc_attn_fn_broadcast was therefore never populated for any
  real (non-dummy) weight load.

Fix: DeepseekV4ForCausalLM.load_weights now calls
self.process_weights_after_loading() before returning, mirroring the
pinned reference's ordering exactly.

Validated with a static/CPU-only test (test_finalize_ordering.py, not
committed): extracts the fixed method's AST, executes it against a fake
AutoWeightsLoader + a call-order-recording fake self, and asserts
AutoWeightsLoader.load_weights runs before process_weights_after_loading,
exactly once, with the original loaded_params return value preserved.
A full end-to-end GPU check happens on next boot.
---
 vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
index ae8132f..88f16fb 100644
--- a/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
+++ b/vllm/models/deepseek_v4/nvidia/model.py
@@ -1541,7 +1541,23 @@ class DeepseekV4ForCausalLM(
 
     def load_weights(self, weights: Iterable[tuple[str, torch.Tensor]]) -> set[str]:
         loader = AutoWeightsLoader(self, skip_substrs=["mtp.", "vision.", "aligner.", "image_", "_vl"])
-        return loader.load_weights(weights, mapper=self.hf_to_vllm_mapper)
+        loaded_params = loader.load_weights(weights, mapper=self.hf_to_vllm_mapper)
+        # Mirror the pinned Vision head (2c8af219) ordering: self-invoke the
+        # post-load finalize step here so it always runs immediately after a
+        # real (non-dummy) weight load, before any forward pass can observe
+        # unfinalized state (e.g. hc_attn_fn_broadcast still None).
+        #
+        # This also matters for the outer VL wrapper
+        # (DeepseekV4ForConditionalGeneration.load_weights, vl_model.py):
+        # it sets `self._weights_finalized = True` right after delegating to
+        # this method, on the assumption that finalization already happened
+        # here. Without this call, that flag was set prematurely, and the
+        # wrapper's own process_weights_after_loading() (the only other
+        # place finalize_mega_moe_weights/finalize_mhc_broadcast_weights
+        # could run) then early-returned and skipped it entirely — so
+        # hc_attn_fn_broadcast was never populated for a real weight load.
+        self.process_weights_after_loading()
+        return loaded_params
 
     def process_weights_after_loading(self) -> None:
         # Model-level post-load hook: runs for every loader, including
